// BT-3130 (ADR 0111 Phase A3): threading-mode matrix — the ADR 0110 shape
// this epic exists to protect against regression: a class-var mutation
// immediately followed by a call that hands off a block whose `^` relays
// out through that call. `generate_field_assignment`'s shadow-write
// (expressions.rs:576-588, `block_depth == 0` gated) must fire for the
// mutation, and the relay must still observe it via the
// `$bt_class_vars_shadow` process-dictionary read (`invoke_class_method/7`).
// Confirmed via `BEAMTALK_CODEGEN_DIAGNOSTICS=1` to emit both a dynamic-
// dispatch diagnostic for the relay call and
// "Non-local return: compiled via throw/catch". Peer:
// `nlr_foreign_relay_actor` (the plain Actor variant with no class var).

Actor subclass: RelayClassCtr
  classState: total = 0

  class helper: aBlock => aBlock value

  // Mutate the class var (shadow-write emitted at block_depth == 0), then
  // hand a block with `^` to a helper class method.
  class mutateThenRelay =>
    self.total := self.total + 1
    self class helper: [^self.total]
    self.total
